      "subtopic": "Two unidirectional associations",
      "basis": "panel",
      "ab3": [],
      "stem": "How many associations, and of what navigability, does this code have between `Person` and `Cat`?\n\n```java\nclass Person {\n    Cat pet;\n}\nclass Cat {\n    Person breeder;\n}\n```",
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "text": "One bidirectional association, because each class refers to the other",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "text": "One unidirectional association from `Person` to `Cat`; the `breeder` field is not an association",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "text": "No associations, only dependencies, because neither link is long-term",
          "correct": false
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "text": "Two unidirectional associations in opposite directions, because the breeder is not necessarily the cat's keeper",
          "correct": true
        }
      ],
      "explanation": "The breeder is not necessarily the person keeping the cat as a pet, so these are two separate associations. Two unidirectional associations in opposite directions do not add up to a single bidirectional association, which needs both objects to point to each other for the same link (as with `pet` and `owner`).",
